# Git Branches

## Naming (with issue — default)

Format: `<type>/issue-<number>-<slug>`

- **type:** `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci` (align with commits)
- **slug:** lowercase English, hyphen-separated, short (e.g. `oauth-login`)

Examples: `feat/issue-42-oauth-login`, `fix/issue-108-null-user-id`

Use after issue triage says **Issue needed** or when implementing an existing `#n`.

## Naming (without issue — exceptions only)

When issue triage says **Skip issue** (typo, single-file trivial, formatting/comments only), issue number is optional:

- `docs/<slug>`
- `chore/<slug>`
- `style/<slug>`

Types `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci` **require** `issue-<number>` in the branch name.

## Default branch

- New repos: use **`main`**.
- Before checkout, PR base, or push: **detect** the repo default branch (`origin/HEAD`, `gh repo view`). If the repo still uses `master`, follow that remote default — do not rename unless the user asks.

## Protected branches

- **Always:** no direct push to the default branch (`main` / `master`). Work on a feature branch → PR → squash merge (see `github-pr`).
- **Template default:** only the default branch is protected.
- **Sub-projects** with `develop`, `staging`, or `release/*` may list extra protected branches in `projects/<name>/.cursor/rules/git-branches.mdc` (same rule: no direct push, use PR).

AI must not `git push origin <default-branch>` unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Lifecycle

| Event | Rule |
|-------|------|
| PR merged | **Delete** the remote branch (GitHub “Delete branch after merge”; see `github-pr`) |
| No activity 30+ days, not merged | Mark as **stale**, **remind** owner; do **not** auto-delete unmerged branches |
| Local cleanup | Periodically `git fetch --prune` |

Optional automation: `templates/github/workflows/stale-branches.yml.example` (reminder only).

## Flow

Issue → `type/issue-<n>-<slug>` → commits → PR (`Fixes #n`) → squash merge → delete branch.

See skill `git-branch-workflow`.
